From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SystemView: steamlike shoulders step one tab at a time

In the system carousel the shoulder buttons (L1/R1) trigger moveCursorFast,
which jumps by manufacturer group (or by 10 when systems are unsorted). With
the steamlike theme's Steam-style top tab bar that skips whole tabs such as
Tools and OpenNOW. Make the shoulders step a single system at a time, but
only when the steamlike theme is active so other themes keep the fast jump.

--- a/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/views/SystemView.cpp
@@ -401,6 +401,15 @@
 					mCarousel.moveSelectionBy(1);
 					return true;
 				}
+				// ROCKNIX steamlike: the Steam-style top tab bar steps one system at a
+				// time on the shoulders (L1/R1). Stock behaviour is a manufacturer (or
+				// x10) "fast jump" that skips tabs such as Tools and OpenNOW; only
+				// override for the steamlike theme so other themes keep the fast jump.
+				if (Settings::getInstance()->getString("ThemeSet") == "steamlike")
+				{
+					if (config->isMappedTo("rightshoulder", input)) { mCarousel.moveSelectionBy(1);  return true; }
+					if (config->isMappedTo("leftshoulder", input))  { mCarousel.moveSelectionBy(-1); return true; }
+				}
 				if ((Settings::getInstance()->getBool("QuickSystemSelect") && config->isMappedLike("down", input)) || config->isMappedTo("rightshoulder", input))
 				{
 					int cursor = moveCursorFast(true);
